            "note": "Rufus's men, counting Odda's sacks for him. They are friendly because friendly is cheaper. Gwyn's dog, if it came along, does not like them and says so."
        },
        {
            "id": "sedges_jar",
            "zone": "lowland",
            "target": "blades",
            "chained": true,
            "once": true,
            "text": "The bog-wife is waiting at a bend of the river road. She presses a stoppered jar into one Blade's hands: for the peddler with the handcart, for his shaking hands. He will be at the fair, he always is. Don't open it.",
            "note": "Mother Sedge's favour for the horse. Ilsa argues for opening it: who carries a stranger's jar unopened? Maren says a promise is a promise. Opened well, it is a tincture for the shakes and nothing worse; opened badly, half of it is spilled, and Sedge will hear through Gwyn that someone looked.",
            "choices": [
                {
                    "id": "carry",
                    "text": "Carry it to the fair.",
                    "keeps": [
                        "word_kept"
                    ],
                    "effects": [
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "carrying_sedges_jar"}
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "open",
                    "text": "Open it.",
                    "breaks": [
                        "word_kept"
                    ],
                    "effects": [
                        {
                            "do": "check",
                            "who": "blades",
                            "ability": "wisdom",
                            "skill": "medicine",
                            "dc": 10,
                            "success": [
                                {"do": "remember", "deed": "opened_sedges_jar"},
                                {"do": "remember", "deed": "carrying_sedges_jar"}
                            ],
                            "failure": [
                                {"do": "remember", "deed": "spilled_sedges_jar"}
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "refuse",
                    "text": "Give it back to her.",
                    "effects": [
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "refused_sedges_jar"}
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "yellow_wagon",
            "zone": "lowland",
            "target": "caravan",
            "owner_pick": "hold",
            "text": "A light wagon with yellow wheels and two fresh horses comes up fast behind. Its driver, a young man in a very good coat, raises his hat and asks Odda to pull onto the verge: first wheat at the fair gets the best price.",
            "note": "Rufus, the Saltmouth factor, buying the harvest on paper before it reaches the fair. Something learned goes out of date: Odda's twenty autumns of being first no longer work, because Rufus's buyers have already signed. If he passes, tell it at the fair as Odda's silence, never as a lesson. Joke: he hands Odda a printed calling card, and she uses it to wedge a sack. Bren admires the horses; Torva knows exactly what kind of man buys debts.",
            "choices": [
                {
                    "id": "let_pass",
                    "text": "Let him pass.",
                    "effects": [
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "let_the_yellow_wagon_pass"}
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "hold",
                    "text": "Keep to the middle of the road.",
                    "effects": [
                        {
                            "do": "check",
                            "who": "blades",
                            "ability": "wisdom",
                            "skill": "animal_handling",
                            "dc": 15,
                            "success": [
                                {"do": "remember", "deed": "held_the_road_against_rufus"}
                            ],
                            "failure": [
                                {"do": "delay", "minutes": 30}
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "for_a_price",
                    "text": "Ask him to pay for the way.",
                    "effects": [
                        {
                            "do": "check",
                            "who": "blades",
                            "ability": "charisma",
                            "skill": "persuasion",
                            "dc": 15,
                            "success": [
                                {
                                    "do": "gain",
                                    "who": "blades",
                                    "copper": 10
                                },
                                {"do": "remember", "deed": "sold_rufus_the_road"}
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "rufus_offer",
            "zone": "lowland",
            "when": "night",
            "target": "blades",
            "once": "contract",
            "text": "After dark a man in a very good coat finds the Blades alone by the horse lines. He is very friendly. Odda's wagon could lose a wheel somewhere quiet tomorrow, he says, and their purses would be heavier for it.",
            "note": "Rufus. The human votes first, as on every card, and the whole table knows this one matters. A blind choice: taking the coin is what Rufus wants his due names at the fair. If Tam or Tobin is riding with the wagon, the fair has heard before Odda pays. Ilsa asks whose rights a contract protects; Bren asks how heavy. Nothing happens to the wheel unless the DM's fight or a later card says so.",
            "choices": [
                {
                    "id": "tell_odda",
                    "text": "Refuse him and tell Odda.",
                    "keeps": [
                        "word_kept"
                    ],
                    "effects": [
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "told_odda_of_rufus"}
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "say_nothing",
                    "text": "Refuse him and say nothing.",
                    "effects": [
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "refused_rufus_quietly"}
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "take",
                    "text": "Take his coin.",
                    "breaks": [
                        "word_kept"
                    ],
                    "effects": [
                        {
                            "do": "gain",
                            "who": "blades",
                            "copper": 50
                        },
                        {"do": "remember", "deed": "took_rufus_coin"}
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "missing_sack",
            "zone": "lowland",
            "target": "caravan",
            "chained": true,
            "once": true,
            "owner_pick": "tracks",
            "text": "Odda counts the sacks twice and her face goes still: one is gone. A passing carter says what the valley always says, that there were roadfolk camped up the road.",
            "note": "The drovers took it, for Rufus. The valley's prejudice is shown and never confirmed: a search of the roadfolk cart finds nothing, and no card makes the roadfolk the culprit. Maren objects to the search out loud. Odda won't search a family's cart on a carter's word. Let it go is Odda's line: \"Bread doesn't argue.\"",
            "choices": [
                {
                    "id": "tracks",
                    "text": "Look for tracks.",
                    "unless": "joined_the_roadfolk_fire",
                    "effects": [
                        {
                            "do": "check",
